  "notes": "{慣習|かんしゅう} means custom or convention - established practices passed down in a society or group.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {慣習|かんしゅう}に{従|したが}う: to follow custom\n- {慣習|かんしゅう}を{守|まも}る: to preserve customs\n- {慣習|かんしゅう}を{破|やぶ}る: to break with convention\n- {社会的|しゃかいてき}{慣習|かんしゅう}: social conventions\n- {慣習|かんしゅう}{法|ほう}: customary law\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {慣習|かんしゅう}: custom, convention (societal practices)\n- {習慣|しゅうかん}: habit (personal, daily routines)\n- {風習|ふうしゅう}: customs, traditional practices (often regional)\n- {伝統|でんとう}: tradition (broader, cultural heritage)\n- {しきたり}: customs, conventions (often unwritten rules)",
